Q. How to install?
Ans. 
  - Make sure to have rust, and cargo(use rustup to install)
  - Set global variable JENNIFER to the directory pointing here
  So, if pwd /home/user/Documents/a/b/jennifer,
  Set JENNIFER=/home/user/Documents/a/b (this is for relative paths)
  - Go to https://download.kiwix.org/zim/wikipedia/, and download some .zim file
  It is better to download things that look like en_*_maxi.all
  If instead of maxi, mini or nopic options are installed the files are smaller
  but images/stylings are not downloaded.
  A good option is this: https://download.kiwix.org/zim/wikipedia/wikipedia_en_computer_maxi_2025-12.zim
  - Create a new folder in this repo called `store`, and copy this .zim file over here
  - Run cargo run --release, things get installed and build, be patient
  - `localhost:8999` should now work

Q. How to download the entire wikipedia?
Ans. 
  Trivial. Download https://download.kiwix.org/zim/wikipedia/wikipedia_en_all_maxi_2026-02.zim (#NOTE: 115G)
  Put it in `store` like before, delete `output` if it exists and cargo run, wait a little
  for everything to compile, and binary zim files to disassemble.

Q. What else can I save offline?
Ans. 
  The openZim project has a large number of projects it maintains offline binary .zim files for.
  Here are all the things you can download-
  - gutenberg
  - wikibooks
  - wikinews
  - wikiquote
  - stack_exchange
  - free_code_camp, etc.
